{
  "Document": [
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Architecture Overview"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Understanding how a Tauri + Leptos application is structured is key to building scalable software. The app is split into two primary environments: the "
        },
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Core Process"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": " and the "
        },
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "WebView Process"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "The Core Process (Rust)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "The Core process is a native Rust application. It has full access to the operating system and is responsible for:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Window management and lifecycle."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Accessing the filesystem, network, and system APIs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Managing global application state."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Handling security and permissions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "The WebView Process (Leptos/WASM)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "The WebView process is where your user interface lives. In this stack, it is a Leptos application compiled to WebAssembly (WASM). It is responsible for:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Rendering the HTML/CSS."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Handling user interactions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Managing local UI state."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "The Bridge (IPC)"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Because the Core and WebView processes are isolated for security reasons, they communicate via "
        },
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Inter-Process Communication (IPC)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ". This bridge allows the frontend to \"invoke\" Rust functions and the backend to \"emit\" events to the UI."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}